2. Toolchain

  - arduino-cli + ESP32 Arduino Core 3.x (FQBN: m5stack:esp32:m5stack_cores3).
    ESP32 Arduino Core is LGPL-2.1. This repository publishes only its own sketch
    sources; it neither ships nor modifies Arduino Core. Normal compiling/linking
    use does not affect this project's MIT licensing.
  - In partitions.csv, the 9.9MB data partition uses subtype 0x83 (littlefs).


3. Trademarks

  M5Stack, CoreS3, Faces, Bottom3 and Keyboard3 are trademarks of M5Stack
  Technology Co., Ltd. This is a personal project with no affiliation or
  partnership with M5Stack.


4. About WorkBuddy

  "WorkBuddy" is a third-party desktop product. The controller app only talks to
  its shortcuts via standard BLE HID keyboard/consumer-control keys and does not
  call any private API. This project is unofficial, unaffiliated and unendorsed.
  The shortcut mapping was verified against the 2026-09 version of WorkBuddy and
  may break after future updates.


5. Optional external dependency (not included, not distributed)

  - media-control (a CLI used on the Mac side to read the "now playing" track,
    installed via Homebrew). Without it the music remote still sends media keys;
    it just won't show title/artwork on screen.


6. Acknowledgements

  - The music remote app (firmware/cores3_shell/app_music.ino and the track-info
    part of mac-bridge/Bridge.swift) takes its overall design from
      isalicema/m5-faces-core-s3 — https://github.com/isalicema/m5-faces-core-s3 (MIT)
    The idea "the device only controls and displays, audio always comes from the
    computer; control goes over HID media keys, now-playing info is pushed back to
    the device screen" comes from that project.
    The implementation here was written independently (NimBLE custom GATT pushing
    title/artist/album/position, artwork sent as a chunked 160x160 JPEG); no code
    was copied. Thanks to the original author for sharing.
  - Product photos in docs/hardware-setup.html come from M5Stack's official docs
    and product pages (docs.m5stack.com); copyright M5Stack Technology Co., Ltd.,
    used here only to illustrate assembly.
